      "message": "It looks like we can use the [\"if this then that\" ayeaye analyzer](http://shortn/_pGPzOksPOY) to make sure these stay in sync with the enum.\n\nSomething like this in `ec_commands.h`:\n\n```\n// LINT.IfChange\nenum fp_capture_type {\n\t/* Full blown vendor-defined capture (produces \u0027frame_size\u0027 bytes) */\n\tFP_CAPTURE_VENDOR_FORMAT \u003d 0,\n\t/* Simple raw image capture (produces width x height x bpp bits) */\n\tFP_CAPTURE_SIMPLE_IMAGE \u003d 1,\n\t/* Self test pattern (e.g. checkerboard) */\n\tFP_CAPTURE_PATTERN0 \u003d 2,\n\t/* Self test pattern (e.g. inverted checkerboard) */\n\tFP_CAPTURE_PATTERN1 \u003d 3,\n\t/* Capture for Quality test with fixed contrast */\n\tFP_CAPTURE_QUALITY_TEST \u003d 4,\n\t/* Capture for pixel reset value test */\n\tFP_CAPTURE_RESET_TEST \u003d 5,\n\tFP_CAPTURE_TYPE_MAX,\n};\n// LINT.ThenChange(/zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_debug.cc)\n```",
      "range": {
